publish-responses-rtt-from-ping-pong

Lane: cross

Unit: measure-websocket-round-trips-with-ping-pong

ChildPatch: publish-responses-rtt-from-ping-pong

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema

Purpose: Expose independent Responses and remote-control WebSocket round-trip observations to the control center for personal ChatGPT accounts.

Requires: none

Provides: Measure matching Ping/Pong round trips for current Plus, Pro and ProLite authentication owners and publish transient connection status; retain Responses observations at thread scope and remote-control observations at app scope, preserving unknown values, real zero, disconnects and account invalidation.

Boundary: Native authentication, relay heartbeats, reconnects and TLS connectors retain their owners. RTT is connection-scoped WebSocket behavior independent of response-attempt recording and atomic output; it does not enter rollout history or relay readiness, and non-personal accounts retain native transport behavior. No private RTT status-line items or setup previews remain. Control-center layout and display formatting remain with its interface consumer.

Verification: Responses Ping/Pong and account-change tests, protocol projection and serialization tests, relay lifecycle tests, and TUI routing, account scope, independent observations, thread replacement and disconnect clearing verify the complete route.

CrossGroup: control-center


